==Strategy==
At long last, you'll face off against Master Uril at the top of the Tower! While he may not offer as big of a challenge as some of the other floors, this retired clan leader is far from a pushover.

Uril may be slow, but he has an Omni-Strike and fires devastating surges, making traditional meatshielding useless. Therefore, you will need to use Crowd Control units like [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] to stall him without needing to meatshield. The combination of [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] are exceptional at this.

Of course, Uril is not without support. Relic peons periodically spawn, and become more common the longer the battle drags on. These peons, especially Sir Rel, can devastate your backline if not dealt with. You will need midrange attackers to deal with them, the anti-Relic [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] are the best at this. These midrange attackers can also help wear down Uril's massive health pool.

Remember to be very careful when using melee units, such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. Try your best to not let them enter Uril's range and become a stepping stone for him to attack and summon a Surge, likely destroying your stack of midrange attackers.

If you have [[Talents|talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] and/or [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]], this stage will be much easier since both units have [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|surge immune]] [[Talents]]. Don't forget to spam other attackers along with other meatshields for the Relic Doges and Sir Rels.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] - This duo is invaluable for keeping the Relic Doges and Sir Rels in check, and can safely attack Uril from a distance.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - One of the best units for controlling Uril. Easily outranges his Omni-Strike and provides Slow procs to control him. Cyberpunk Cat's Slow talent is strongly recommended.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] - Works well with Cyberpunk Cat. Helps cover Cyberpunk's slow downtime while pushing Uril back.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] - The on-demand Slow and Knockback against Uril is always appreciated. Do note he does not have Curse Immunity, so you'll need to time him well.
*[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] - Tourist Cat can help you regain a lot of ground against Uril. Uril will eventually use them as a stepping stone for his surge, so only use them when you really need to push Uril back. Also be careful as Tourist Cat is vulnerable to Curse.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - There are no Dark enemies here, but his good generalist stats & Area Attack make him a good option to use alongside Slapsticks Cats, further assisting with the peons and chipping down Uril.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] - Jelly Dumpling Cat is absolutely invaluable as an attacker, as it has exactly enough range and foreswing to hit the Sir Rels and Relic Doges without support, allowing it to take huge chunks out of the peon waves. If possible, try to let the peons knock it out so that it does not become a stepping stone for Uril.
*[[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Gato Amigo]] - Default option for stalling Uril on anti-Surge strategies, with his cheap cost and spammability being useful.
*[[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Li'l King Dragon Cat]] - The go-to midrange attacker for anti-Surge strategies, providing decent DPS though he would need assistance for the Relic peons. However, he is still outranges by Uril's normal attack's Omni-Strike, which can two-shot him even with level 50 and a high amount of + levels.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] - A strong option, especially as an alternative to Sniper the Deadeye. Jagando can constantly knock back Uril and dish out decent anti-traitless damage. He also has Strong Against and a Surge Immunity to last a while against Uril. However, he is extremely weak to the Relic Peons, so try your best to support him.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] - Bullet Train Cat can be used as a burst of damage against Uril or more commonly a peon. Use it carefully, for it will surely become a stepping stone for Uril to fire off a surge.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - You'll need to pair him with constant anti-Traitless CC, but he can pay off by chaining multiple attacks doing an enormous amount of total damage per use. He can also be used as an emergency button to wipe off all peons.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]]: Can protect Slapstick and Jagando from Relic peons while also avoiding becoming a stepping stone for Uril, thanks to having just a bit less but still very similar range. Doguemon also has high attack power to chip Uril or defeat the peons, and can resist a bit of Uril's damage, though still vulnerable to Surges.
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Ironcat]]: With his Weaken and Resistance to Traitless, immunity to Surge and Curse and tons of knockbacks to re-apply the Weaken, Ironcat is perfect for stalling Uril on his own when no Relic peons are present. Beware though, with Ironcat constantly within his range, Uril will have the opportunity to spawn many Surges.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]: Think of him as a better, specialized Slapsticks that can juggle Sir Rels efficiently unlike Slapsticks with their somewhat sluggish attack rate, while boasting Massive Damage against Relics to quickly remove them ASAP.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]] - Aphrodite is a very good choice on Sniperpunk strategies. She can comfortably outrange Uril's omni-strike and surges while dishing out constant, strong DPS and helping with the peons. At level 38 and above, she can knock out the Sir Rels in a single attack.
*[[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Talented Mad Doctor Klay]] - Mad Doctor Klay, with his Target Traitless and Surge Immune talents will trivialise this stage. Klay can outrange Uril's standing range and have his monster do enough damage to knock back Uril with each slam.
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]] - Assassinlan pairs very well with Cyberpunk and Sniper the Deadeye, providing yet another slow proc. It also has a [[Long-Legged (Combo)|two-slot Medium Slow combo]] to further strengthen your lineup's control ability.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]] - Lunos is an amazing tank with a short cooldown, and with his conjure, is able to chip away at Uril. And with his double bounty, he's able to sustain a stable enough cash flow to afford another Lunos a bit after the one falls. Be wary of his lack of surge immunity.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Merc]] - With her repeated Freeze procs against both Relic and Traitless enemies, she proves to be an extremely good choice when coupled with units like Tourist Cat and Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - As the legend says, whatever Cosmo outranges will be reduced to ash. Using him with Sniper the Deadeye or Macho Crystal Cat is very risky, since it makes him clip into Uril's Surge and kill himself. His high damage output + Wave Attack is enough to make this risk worthwhile, and with support, he can juggle Uril with every attack.

